From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcm80, msvcm90, msvcp60..120: Exports of existing functions.

Spec stubs of the older C++ runtimes whose functions already exist:
msvcm80 and msvcm90 entries forward to msvcp80/msvcp90 (the native C++
library functions, and the C functions behind their mangled managed
copies), 223 + 144 entries; msvcp70 gets the complex<float>/<double>
operators, basic_ostream uninitialized constructors, ostrstream and string
iterator members its sources already build (135 entries); msvcp71/80 the
basic_ostream uninitialized constructors; msvcp60..90 _LCosh/_LSinh;
msvcp110 and msvcp120 _Throw_Cpp_error, which throws the same thread errors
as in msvcp140 (the function now builds for 110+).
---
 dlls/msvcm80/msvcm80.spec   | 446 ++++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 dlls/msvcm90/msvcm90.spec   | 288 ++++++++++++++--------------
